body:
Queue: core, position 16.

## Context
Judges read the README when the repo goes public. Craig pastes the submission text into the event's submission, whose method is not stated (`docs/JUDGING.md` section 6). Both are judge-facing copy: no typed numbers, no em dashes, plain words, and the Torus guardrails. Milestone: Train 8 (draft by Train 6).

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] The README covers:
  - what Clearlane is;
  - how to run it offline (`npm ci`, `npm run build`, `npx vite preview`);
  - the six beats;
  - what is real (one row per provenance class);
  - data sources and licenses: CAISO OASIS, EIA, Torus pages by URL, and Open-Meteo CC BY 4.0 for the `slc_*` columns (or those columns dropped);
  - the limits: CO2 is average emissions; the heatmap states no time zone, so both readings show; 500 MW is an MOU ceiling; host results are in kW; the fleet is assumed not to move prices; stations are simulated Torus-style;
  - how it was built: a solo founder, six agent lanes, issues and PRs on GitHub.
- [ ] Every README number comes from a block between `<!-- numbers:start -->` and `<!-- numbers:end -->`, written from `numbers.json` by `tools/readme-numbers.mjs`, or from a link to `docs/NUMBERS.md` if `reproduce` merged.
- [ ] `demo/submission.md` has plain text ready to paste:
  - title;
  - one-line summary;
  - short description;
  - bounty: Torus only;
  - team: Craig, solo;
  - repo URL;
  - the video and deck file names.

  Craig submits it.
- [ ] Copy rules: no em dash; American English; no hype words; "not advertised", never "Torus lacks"; "value to RMP's system at day-ahead prices".
- [ ] Grok's guardrail review is handled.
- [ ] Both files are re-checked after the Oct 28 refresh and at Train 8.

## Files touched
- `README.md`
- `demo/submission.md`
- `tools/readme-numbers.mjs`

## How to verify
```bash
node tools/readme-numbers.mjs && git diff --stat README.md
grep -n "—" README.md demo/submission.md   # expect no output
grep -niE "comprehensive|robust|seamless|leverage|cutting-edge|game-changer|torus lacks" README.md demo/submission.md   # expect no output
node tools/facts-check.mjs
```

## Dependencies
The fact ledger.

Brief: `docs/lanes/integration.md`.
